0.1.6 (2026-11-06)
  * ORDER 437 (review of 252c): no Cisco VPNC row (network-manager-vpnc has left Debian testing, so it could never be offered). The rescue entry brings GPart, Partclone, FSArchiver, nwipe and Sparky Chrooter, the tools the image does not install: it named TestDisk and ddrescue, which the system task depends on, so removing the entry would have removed the task (study J23).

0.1.5 (2026-11-06)
  * ORDER 252c (study items J9, J26, J27): a VPN section offers the plain NetworkManager plugins (OpenVPN, OpenConnect, L2TP/IPsec, strongSwan, PPTP, SSH tunnel), never the GNOME editors; a Tools section offers Syncthing with its Plasma widget, Vorta with Borg, KeePassXC, Solaar, Piper, Yakuake, the rescue tools (TestDisk, ddrescue, Sparky Chrooter) and HPLIP, which shows only while Debian offers it. Paweł's own VPN page is his package's file and stays as it ships.
  * An entry may name companions (`also`): installed, removed and offered together, and shown only when every package of the entry is offered.
  * The two section titles in the 21 languages of the page.

0.1.4 (2026-11-04)
  * Show, beside an entry that is not installed, the install-time downloads it brings (the packages apt would install for it whose control file declares Sparky-Install-Download-Size and Sparky-Install-Download-Source), with size and source, on a metered connection and, said, when NetworkManager cannot be read (ORDER 399b; Daniel, 2026-11-04: "warn the user with current size on stereo aptus interface or apt"). One declaration and one reader, shared with apt's own notice (sparky-stereo-apt 20261104.3, which this version depends on), in the nine languages.
  * FlightGear joins the catalogue (stereo programs section): its data downloader declares 1.75 GiB.

